{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc9a262bb15f1a19e63adaa560496b85859a6f29741524","commits":["526784c00925eb86505c47c7bf493d368517fed9","c8c809bf14e984984ac75cfeffccc94c1696d65a","c0f50a7db523279d0312c4a551cf99632a75c8b8","38a8717c09e280544eeee7fb26ff5a8b9c08f435"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**miniclaude is now a Go program.** The Python package and the npm shim are gone: install it with `go install github.com/stricttools/miniclaude@v0`, or from the Linux and macOS archives on each GitHub Release. Nothing newer than 0.3.0 is published to PyPI or npm, and 0.3.0 stays there. Python and prompt_toolkit are no longer needed; the fullscreen terminal layer is miniclaude's own.","type":"breaking"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc9a2636e872788769298abc0c4bf2905227a4d34b3aac","commits":["6a7d8cb60f9d6332d3938974bf2817d5f266599a"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Sessions start Claude Code through claudewheel.** The REPL runs Claude Code as `claudewheel profile exec`, through claudestream 0.16.0, so it needs a claudewheel that has the `profile exec` command.","type":"breaking"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc9a263e1de9a4ea60dca32b30433c9186b2be4d91965c","commits":["38a8717c09e280544eeee7fb26ff5a8b9c08f435","cffddcbbd9223b3e51c15ec86dd0dbb99a8ad24c"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Command line additions.** `repl` takes `--claude-binary` and `--claudewheel-binary`, absolute paths of the programs (looked up on PATH when omitted); `history import` converts the old history file; `mock` shows its seed as the first output line, and its `dialogs` command also opens a dialog the REPL does not support. `repl` and `mock` refuse `--json` and refuse to run without a terminal on standard input and output.","type":"feature"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc9a26459951ed547b8f3a70bc46e2b7667cd1a52030be","commits":["6f8e0ce716862af8f9e36cec14ea52cf8ce031f1","2b78263efd5220c664a3cf1b2c84637621f04bec"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**The REPL keeps going when one thing fails.** A failing `/model`, `/mode`, or `/context` is a red error line instead of ending the REPL; an event that cannot be shown is reported as a red line, and a request that cannot be shown is denied with the reason, instead of ending the turn and leaving Claude Code waiting; a failed interrupt is shown instead of swallowed; a failing howmuchleft is a red line naming the reason instead of stale status rows; and a hung-up terminal (SIGHUP) is restored before miniclaude exits.","type":"fix"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc9a264cbdd6e882ac62e4ecde4ed298cf1bab13a992d0","commits":["952c757c313ebecaac24e4dde710138fdc3b2633"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Tables stay below the text before them.** A table no longer appears above the paragraph that preceded it when both arrived in the same chunk of the stream; output is the same however the stream is split.","type":"fix"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc9a2654267b7ee95a825d64144df68478a32fdd005ee1","commits":["1f6ed5e1e69c123a6936e57975b6a5b4b8ad4149","ada5d708de08e1dd558da4afb522161622850cdf","c4f360d3313e21eef7455be1f74c645e97738e9b"],"user_facing":false}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc9a277a24ba1f2c0811ec2fcf42d7bb89a3a3e9ab8d15","commits":["0574ae51f6b53c74e2b021a716cdcd750fa1ba1e","2b3c9613b9113cda0e7854c3ac46c7726bce47a0"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**The prompt history moves.** Submitted prompts are kept as JSON lines in `$XDG_STATE_HOME/miniclaude/history.jsonl` (`~/.local/state/miniclaude/history.jsonl` when it is unset), not in `~/.miniclaude/history`. Carry the old history over once with `miniclaude history import --from ~/.miniclaude/history`, which refuses when the new file exists.","type":"breaking"}
